1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,860
Have you ever loved a TV show?
你曾经热爱过一部电视剧吗？

2
00:00:03,860 --> 00:00:06,670
I mean really loved it?
我是说真的热爱？

3
00:00:06,670 --> 00:00:11,750
Like, you can't wait to get to work to talk about it loved it?
就像，你迫不及待地想去上班，就为了和别人谈论它的那种热爱？

4
00:00:11,750 --> 00:00:14,210
What about the cliffhanger?
那扣人心弦的悬念呢？

5
00:00:14,210 --> 00:00:20,850
That‘s the unresolved situation at the end of the episode which makes you want to watch the next one.
就是一集结尾处那个悬而未决的情节，让你忍不住想看下一集。

6
00:00:20,850 --> 00:00:24,260
But, when will the next one be?
但是，下一集什么时候才会播出呢？

7
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:30,920
In the past, viewers had to wait up to a week for the next episode of their favourite shows.
在过去，观众们不得不等上长达一周的时间，才能看到他们最喜欢的电视剧的下一集。

8
00:00:30,920 --> 00:00:32,590
What agony!
这是多么痛苦啊！

9
00:00:32,590 --> 00:00:35,940
But, that's not the case any more.
但是，现在情况不再是这样了。

10
00:00:35,940 --> 00:00:44,120
And hand in hand with that comes a, possibly dangerous, growing social trend.
与此同时，一种可能危险的、日益增长的社会趋势也随之而来。

11
00:00:44,120 --> 00:00:46,940
We speak of binge-watching.
我们把它叫做疯狂追剧。

12
00:00:46,940 --> 00:00:54,270
Binge-watching is when a person watches more than one episode of a show in quick succession.
疯狂追剧指的是一个人接连不断地观看一部电视剧的多集内容。

13
00:00:54,270 --> 00:01:10,790
With developments in the speed and connectivity of the internet, increases in technology and the rise of on-demand entertainment companies, people can now have their favourite shows streamed directly to their television at their convenience.
随着互联网网速和连接性的发展、技术的进步以及点播娱乐公司的兴起，人们现在可以在方便的时候，将他们喜欢的电视剧直接流式传输到他们的电视上观看。

14
00:01:10,790 --> 00:01:14,090
This behaviour is nothing new.
这种行为并不是什么新鲜事。

15
00:01:14,090 --> 00:01:20,160
In fact, 'binge-watching' has been officially listed in dictionaries since 2015.
事实上，“疯狂追剧”自2015年起就已被正式收录进词典。

16
00:01:20,160 --> 00:01:26,520
The entertainment companies recognise this behaviour and many take steps to encourage it.
娱乐公司认识到了这种行为，并且很多公司都采取措施来鼓励它。

17
00:01:26,520 --> 00:01:35,200
Often, instead of releasing each episode on a week-by-week basis, an entire series will become available concurrently.
通常，一整部电视剧会同时上线，而不是每周播出一集。

18
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:45,270
Once the episode finishes, many platforms will display pop-ups with 'you might like' suggestions, or will automatically play the next episode.
一集结束后，许多平台会显示带有“你可能喜欢”推荐内容的弹出窗口，或者会自动播放下一集。

19
00:01:45,270 --> 00:01:51,130
However, this wondrous gift may in fact be a poisoned chalice.
然而，这份奇妙的礼物实际上可能是一个看似诱人实则有害的事物。

20
00:01:51,130 --> 00:01:59,150
Recent research from British media watchdog Ofcom suggests that this behaviour may have become a hindrance.
英国媒体监管机构英国通信管理局最近的研究表明，这种行为可能已经成为了一种阻碍。

21
00:01:59,150 --> 00:02:16,370
Out of the more than half of British adults who watch more than one episode of a show back-to-back, almost a third have admitted missing sleep or becoming tired as a result; and one quarter have neglected their household chores.
在超过一半连续观看多集电视剧的英国成年人中，几乎三分之一的人承认因此而睡眠不足或感到疲惫；四分之一的人忽视了他们的家务。

22
00:02:16,370 --> 00:02:19,190
Next we'll be missing work!
接下来我们可能连工作都要耽误了！

23
00:02:19,190 --> 00:02:25,670
Bingeing has other connections — binge eating, binge drinking and binge smoking.
疯狂追剧还与其他行为有关——暴饮暴食、酗酒和大量吸烟。

24
00:02:25,670 --> 00:02:33,840
All of which are often associated with compulsive behaviour, a lack of control and a possible route to addiction.
所有这些行为通常都与强迫性行为、缺乏自控力以及可能导致成瘾相关。

25
00:02:33,840 --> 00:02:48,720
Lindsey Fussell, consumer group director at Ofcom, said: "The days of waiting a week for the next episode are largely gone, with people finding it hard to resist watching multiple episodes around the house or on the move."
英国通信管理局的消费者团体主管林赛·富塞尔说：“等上一周看下一集的日子在很大程度上已经一去不复返了，人们发现无论是在家里还是在外出途中，都很难抗拒连续观看多集电视剧。”

26
00:02:48,720 --> 00:03:01,990
If people find binge-watching hard to resist, coupled with the fact that it has shown to lead to negligence in many, are we witnessing the birth of a new type of addiction?
如果人们发现疯狂追剧难以抗拒，再加上它已经被证明会导致很多人做事粗心大意，那么我们是否正在见证一种新型成瘾行为的诞生呢？

27
00:03:01,990 --> 00:03:11,390
The myriad of information and entertainment that television and online media can bring us is, many would say, a good thing.
许多人会说，电视和网络媒体能够带给我们的海量的信息和娱乐是一件好事。

28
00:03:11,390 --> 00:03:19,710
It offers us opportunities to better understand the world we live in, educate ourselves and enjoy much needed downtime.
它为我们提供了更好地了解我们所生活的世界、自我教育以及享受非常需要的休闲时光的机会。

29
00:03:19,710 --> 00:03:26,210
However, like any behaviour done to excess, it can become dangerous.
然而，就像任何过度的行为一样，它也可能变得危险。

30
00:03:26,210 --> 00:03:34,520
And when the activity begins to bleed into other areas, causing us to stop functioning — then it becomes a problem.
当这种行为开始渗透到其他领域，导致我们无法正常生活时——那么它就成了一个问题。

31
00:03:34,520 --> 00:03:36,440
So, what's the answer?
那么，解决办法是什么呢？

32
00:03:36,440 --> 00:03:37,940
Moderation!
适度！

33
00:03:37,940 --> 00:03:40,890
Neither a tiny amount, nor too much.
既不要太少，也不要太多。

34
00:03:40,890 --> 00:03:46,540
After all, as the old proverb says... a little of what you fancy does you good.
毕竟，正如那句古老的谚语所说......喜欢的东西，稍微享受一点对你有好处。
